---
// src/pages/maria-montessori.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Maria Montessori"
  description="Learn about Dr. Maria Montessori — the pioneering educator who founded the Montessori Method over a century ago."
>

  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About Maria Montessori</p>
      <h1>About Maria Montessori</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead">
        The visionary educator whose method has shaped childhood for over a century.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bio Section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="bio-block">

        <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:2rem; margin-bottom:2rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <div style="flex-shrink:0; width:90px; height:90px; border-radius:50%; background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--color-secondary),var(--color-primary)); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:3.5rem; box-shadow:var(--shadow-md);">👩‍🔬</div>
          <div>
            <h2 style="color:var(--color-primary); margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Dr. Maria Montessori</h2>
            <p style="color:var(--color-text-muted); font-size:0.92rem; margin-bottom:0; max-width:none;">1870–1952 · Chiaravalle, Italy · Physician &amp; Educator</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          Maria Montessori was born in 1870, Chiaravalle, Italy. Montessori was the first woman
          to graduate from University of Roma La Sapienza and became the <strong>first female
          doctor in Italy</strong>. Through her scientific observation and medical practice, she
          studied how children learn and established that education is not what the teacher gives
          but is a process that is spontaneously carried out by what an individual finds in the
          environment that surrounds him/her.
        </p>

        <p>
          In 1907, she founded the first school for children called
          <strong>"Casa dei Bambini"</strong> or <strong>"Children's House"</strong>. Through
          her observation, she developed specialized material which enabled children to absorb
          knowledge effortlessly from their surroundings. There she developed what is now known
          as the <strong>"Montessori Method"</strong> or <strong>"Montessori Approach"</strong>,
          which focuses on quality rather than quantity. The success of her school created
          interest in surrounding countries and is now internationally known.
        </p>

        <p>
          Since her creation began, there have been many associations created in her name. Some
          have altered her methods and amalgamated them with other philosophies. At Monkey Tree
          Montessori Preschool, we follow what Dr. Montessori created over a hundred years ago.
          It is a method that has lasted over a century and continues to gain popularity from
          its success.
        </p>

      </div>

      <!-- Quote -->
      <div class="quote-block">
        <blockquote>
          "The greatest sign of success for a teacher is to be able to say, 'The children are now working as if I did not exist.'"
        </blockquote>
        <cite>— Dr. Maria Montessori</cite>
      </div>

      <!-- Timeline / Key Facts -->
      <div style="margin-top:3rem; max-width:860px; margin-inline:auto;">
        <h2 style="color:var(--color-primary); text-align:center; margin-bottom:2rem;">Key Milestones</h2>
        <div class="grid-2">

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">🎓</span>
            <h4 class="card__title">1870 — Born in Italy</h4>
            <p class="card__body">Born on August 31 in Chiaravalle, Italy. Showed exceptional academic ability from an early age.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">👩‍⚕️</span>
            <h4 class="card__title">1896 — First Female Doctor</h4>
            <p class="card__body">Became Italy's first female physician after graduating from the University of Rome La Sapienza.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">🏫</span>
            <h4 class="card__title">1907 — Casa dei Bambini</h4>
            <p class="card__body">Founded the first "Children's House" in Rome's San Lorenzo district, serving children ages 3–6.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">🌐</span>
            <h4 class="card__title">1920s–40s — Global Spread</h4>
            <p class="card__body">The Montessori Method spread across Europe, the Americas, and Asia — gaining international recognition.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Our Commitment -->
  <section class="section--alt section" style="padding-block:3.5rem;">
    <div class="container" style="text-align:center; max-width:760px; margin-inline:auto;">
      <h2 style="color:var(--color-primary); margin-bottom:1rem;">Our Commitment to Authentic Montessori</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--color-text-muted); font-size:1.05rem;">
        At Monkey Tree, we honour Dr. Montessori's original vision. We follow the method she
        created over a hundred years ago — unchanged and uncompromised — because it works.
      </p>
      <div style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <a href="/curriculum" class="btn btn--primary">Explore Our Curriculum</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
